# Chapter brief: 14-extending-the-semantics.md

## Objective
Write `experiments/zkir-k/docs/14-extending-the-semantics.md`, a complete chapter of about 1400 words (tables and code blocks not counted).

## Persona
Write as: Maintainer and K expert who writes the contributor guide with checklists and worked examples. The persona shapes emphasis and examples only; the hard rules of the common brief still apply, and the text must never mention the persona.

## Must cover
- Conventions of the definition: `symbol(_)` on every constructor, `[function, total]` with `[owise]` fallbacks, explicit `requires` guards, `[priority(30)]` for the extension overrides, sequential helper chains (`#recon..#recon4`, `#lt..#lt4`) and why sequential resolution matters, error-string fidelity to the crate, the split between witness rules and gate evaluation.
- Checklist for adding an instruction: syntax constructor, reads/writes, wf arity, off-circuit function in zkir-ops.k, VM rule, gate evaluation rule, chip requirement, preprocessor mapping in zkir_kast.py, error class in diff_test.py, a handmade program, a unit check, a divergence case if the two sides differ. Illustrate with an existing instruction traced through every file.
- Checklist for adding a type; checklist for adding a chip.
- Pitfalls encountered in this definition and how to avoid them (read CONSOLIDATED.md and the K best-practices wiki page): duplicate function definitions across modules, owise overlap, parse ambiguities, catch-all rules that hide unsupported cases, stuck configurations reported as success, symbolic unfolding of hashes on the Haskell backend.
- How to re-run the check layers after a change, and the receipts to update.

## Verification before you finish
- Re-read every claim that names a file, a symbol, a number or a message and confirm it against the source.
- Confirm every command you show runs from the repository root (run it if it is read-only and quick).
- Confirm the file has no placeholder, no TODO, no mention of drafting or reviewing, and exactly one `#` title.

When the chapter is written and verified, reply with one line: DONE experiments/zkir-k/docs/14-extending-the-semantics.md <word count>.
